    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe create audit line is emitted by `AuditOwnerCreated` (wired as the `audit` step in `owners.POST.yml`, right after `save`). It previously logged only `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, keeping the existing fields:\n\n```java\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper) {\n    AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n            ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner).getMembershipLevel(), owner.getMembershipNumber());\n}\n```\n\nKey points:\n- `membershipNumber` is a stored field on `Owner` (assigned earlier in the POST pipeline by `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`), read directly.\n- `membershipLevel` is a *derived* value \u2014 not stored on the entity \u2014 so I obtain it the same way the response does, via the injected `OwnerMapper` (`toOwnerDto(owner).getMembershipLevel()`). OfficeFloor injects the mapper bean by type, exactly as `RespondWithOwnerCreated` already does. This guarantees the audited level matches the value the test reads back from the fetched owner (a newly created owner has zero tenure, so the level is identical at create and immediate fetch).\n\nVerified: `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes and the audit line now reads e.g. `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-08-14 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`. `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
